# Spring-NWVMC (`0.1.0`) Cursor Rules (SDD + TDD Enabled)

This repository uses **Spring-NWVMC (`io.github.natswarchuan:spring-nwvmc:0.1.0` on Maven Central; optional JitPack `v0.1.0`)** on **Java 21 LTS + Spring Boot 3.x**.
For full attribute matrices, 40 auto-endpoints, YAML properties, verified recipes, non-annotation class imports, and the SDD/TDD playbook, read `.agents/skills/spring-nwvmc-adoption/SKILL.md`, `references/01..06`, and `templates/{spec,plan,tasks}.template.md` before inventing syntax.

## Mandatory SDD (Spec-Driven) & TDD (Test-Driven) Workflow
- **SDD First:** Before coding a new feature, draft `specs/<feature>/spec.md` (`REQ-ID` Given/When/Then criteria, schema, API surface, security/RBAC/tenant rules, NFRs). Pause on any `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION]` item until confirmed, then write `plan.md` (Traceability Matrix) & `tasks.md` (`[RED]→[GREEN]→[REFACTOR]`). Keep `spec.md` synced with live `/v3/api-docs` and `/schema/zod`. *(Small tweaks/prototypes: lightweight mini-spec + 1 `MockMvc`/regression test.)*
- **TDD Red → Green → Refactor:** Write a failing JUnit 5 / `MockMvc` test (`@DisplayName("REQ-XXX: ...")`) BEFORE production code (and failing regression test first for every bug fix), observe RED failure, implement minimal declarative Spring-NWVMC code until GREEN, then REFACTOR. NEVER weaken assertions or add `@Disabled`. Verify all 4 tiers (Unit, `MockMvc` Integration, Contract Drift, Concurrency/JMeter).

## Architecture & Build Requirements
- Require Java 21 LTS, Maven Central `io.github.natswarchuan:spring-nwvmc:0.1.0`, and `<parameters>true</parameters>` in `maven-compiler-plugin`.
- Follow the **2-Directory Contract**:
  - `entity/`: JPA `@Entity` extending `BaseAuditEntity` (UUIDv7 `id`, soft-delete, audit columns, `@Version` optimistic locking built-in — NEVER invent `@SoftDelete`, NEVER use Lombok `@Data` on `@Entity`).
  - `controller/`: `@AutoRestController` Java `interface` extending `AutoApiController<E>` (40 endpoints) or narrow composable interfaces (`AutoReadApi<E>`, `AutoKeysetApi<E>`, `AutoAnalyticsApi<E>`, `AutoSchemaApi<E>`, `AutoWriteApi<E>`, `AutoBatchApi<E>`, `AutoExportImportApi<E>`, `AutoWorkflowApi<E>`, `AutoAiApi<E>`).
- Do NOT generate redundant CRUD repositories, services, or concrete `@RestController` classes for entities managed by `@AutoRestController`.

## Exact 6 Real Annotation Packages (Zero Fictional Annotations)
1. `io.github.natswarchuan.core.annotation.*` (54 annotations)
2. `io.github.natswarchuan.module.cache.http.annotation.HttpCacheable`
3. `io.github.natswarchuan.module.datasource.annotation.{TargetDataSource, TargetDatabasePlatform}`
4. `io.github.natswarchuan.module.event.annotation.PublishCloudEvent`
5. `io.github.natswarchuan.module.lock.annotation.DistributedLock`
6. `io.github.natswarchuan.module.webhook.annotation.EntityWebhook`

## Empirically Verified Runtime Pitfalls (NEVER Violate)
- **`@StateMachine.transitions`:** Colon syntax `"CREATED:PENDING_PAYMENT,CANCELLED"`, NEVER `"FROM -> TO"`. Invoke via `POST /api/v1/{entity}/{id}/transition?targetState=...`, NEVER JSON body.
- **Query Operators:** Dot syntax (`retailPrice.gte=1000&productName.like=MacBook`), NEVER `__gte`.
- **CamelCase Base Paths:** `ECommerceOrder` → `/api/v1/e-commerce-orders`. Set `@AutoRestController(basePath = "...")` if custom URI needed.
- **`ObjectProvider<T>` Injection:** Consumer `@Component` / `@Service` beans injecting framework `@AutoComponent` helpers (`DynamicEntityAiMetadataProviderHelper`, `AiNaturalLanguageQueryParserHelper`, `ThirdPartyRestClientHelper`, `WebhookDispatcherHelper`) MUST inject `ObjectProvider<T>` and call `.getObject()` at runtime.
- **`@Lazy` Non-Final Services + Lazy Injection:** Consumer `@Service` beans using `@DistributedLock`, `@AutoCacheable`, `@AutoCacheEvict`, or `@TargetDataSource` MUST be **non-final** and **`@Lazy`**, AND callers injecting them MUST use **`ObjectProvider<MyService>`** or **`@Lazy`** (`0.1.0` supports method-level `@TargetDataSource` natively). NEVER put `@Transactional` on `public final class` Helpers. Use `HttpHeaderConstant.HEADER_X_IDEMPOTENCY_KEY` for `"X-Idempotency-Key"`.
- **Dev JWT & Testing:** Use `POST /api/v1/auth/token?username=admin&role=ROLE_ADMIN` (NOT `/system/studio/demo-token`) and `JwtTokenService.generateToken(username, userId, roles)` (`username` FIRST!).
- **`readDto` Scoping:** Controllers declaring `readDto = X.class` project ALL responses through `X`. Mount endpoints returning custom DTOs on a controller without `readDto`.
- **Custom Route Security:** `@ServiceOverride` custom methods default to `writeRoles` (fail-closed); `@CustomEndpoint` dispatches directly to the delegated Spring bean (place security/AOP on the bean).
- **Outbox & Storage:** Outbox event types use `EventConstant` (`ENTITY_CREATED`); `POST /api/v1/storage/upload` returns `201 Created`.

## Production Security Lockdown
- Keep `app.framework.studio.enabled: false`, `demo-token-endpoint-enabled: false`, `fail-fast-weak-jwt-secret: true`, and `JWT_SECRET >= 32` UTF-8 bytes in `application.yml` / `application-prod.yml`. Enable Studio ONLY in `application-dev.yml`.
- Annotate every protected entity with `@EntitySecurity(...)` and mask sensitive columns with `@FieldSecurity(...)`.
- Before finishing, verify against `.agents/skills/spring-nwvmc-adoption/CHECKLIST.md` and run `mvn clean verify` (`0` failures, `0` `@Disabled`).
